# Lab stack — relay-edge + relay-pubsub + Relay (+ optional Forge)
# Copy and source before running stack scripts FROM YOUR WORKSTATION:
#   cp config/lab-stack.env.example config/lab-stack.env
#   # fill RELAY_AUTH_TOKEN; FORGE_* only when Forge is deployed
#   set -a && source config/lab-stack.env && set +a
#   ./scripts/e2e-stack.sh
#
# IMPORTANT — remote hosts (default):
#   Relay, relay-pubsub, and relay-edge may each run on a DIFFERENT machine.
#   BASE / GATEWAY / EDGE must be the reachable host URLs for those services.
#   Do NOT use https://127.0.0.1:… here when testing from your laptop — that
#   only hits localhost on the machine running the script.
#
#   127.0.0.1 is only correct inside a service’s own env when its peer is on
#   the SAME host (e.g. Relay RELAY_ACTION_TARGETS → co-located pubsub).
#
# No Forge:  ./scripts/e2e-stack.sh
# With Forge: fill FORGE_* below + RELAY_FORGE_* on Relay process, then ./scripts/e2e-forge-stack.sh
#
# Example all-on-one labs (still use the public host IP from your laptop):
#   212.8.248.187 — Relay :8443 · pubsub :8081 · console :8082 · edge :18086
#   175.110.122.71 — Relay :18080 · pubsub :8081 · console :8082 · edge :18086
#     → or use config/lab-stack-175.env.example
#
# Split example (each project remote):
#   BASE=https://relay.example:8443
#   GATEWAY=https://pubsub.example:8081
#   EDGE=https://edge.example:18086
#
# EDGE is usually https:// when EDGE_TLS=1 (remote deploy default).
# RELAY_FORGE_* must be set on the Relay process (not relay-edge).
# After Relay restart, re-sync relay-pubsub RELAY_AUTH_TOKEN (same demo login JWT).

BASE=https://<relay-host>:8443
GATEWAY=https://<gateway-host>:8081
EDGE=https://<edge-host>:18086
FORGE_BASE=
FORGE_API_KEY=
RELAY_AUTH_TOKEN=
RELAY_TLS_INSECURE=1
RELAY_DEMO_USER=demo
RELAY_DEMO_PASSWORD=demo
PROJECT=fasal-onprem
